--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT PATH (literal prompt path used — no drift, covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/**`. Unlike the
earlier EnergyFlow note, that path IS now a real, compiled project.yml source group: `project.yml`
lists `TeslaSync/Features` as a source path for both the iOS (`TeslaSync`) and macOS
(`TeslaSync-macOS`) app targets (createIntermediateGroups: true), and landed sibling P7 pages already
ship under it (TeslaSync/Features/VehicleSystems/TirePressurePage.swift,
TeslaSync/Features/Trips/TripsReplayPage.swift, …). So the page is written at the literal prompt path
and compiles into the `TeslaSync` module alongside the shared P2/P3 library in `Sources/`.

The web route `/power-flow` had NO `AppRoute` case (only the sidebar/breadcrumb string referenced it);
this prompt adds `.powerFlowDashboard` (pathSegment `power-flow`, group `.energy`, systemImage
`bolt.horizontal.fill`) to `Sources/App/AppRoute.swift` so `AppRouteParser` resolves `/power-flow`
+ the deep link automatically, and wires the host in `Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift`
(`PowerFlowDashboardRouteRegistration.registry`). ("navigation registration" is an allowed file class.)

SYMBOL-COLLISION NOTE (covenant #1): the dashboard-widget namespace already ships `PowerFlowStrings`
(PowerFlowHistoryWidget.Model.swift) and `PowerFlowFormat` (LivePowerFlowWidget.Model.swift), plus a
`FlowArrow` struct and a crowded set of `PowerFlow*` widget types. Every type this unit introduces is
therefore prefixed `PowerFlowDashboard*` (or the unique domain names `TeslaEnergyLiveStatus[Sample]`);
a full-module declaration scan confirms zero redeclarations against the existing widget symbols.

