--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISPOSITION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI PowerFlowDashboardPage shipped at full parity with the web source: a
pure @Observable PowerFlowDashboardPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing
loading / error / ready over an injectable PowerFlowDashboardDataSource seam whose three methods keep
the web hook names (useTeslaEnergyLiveStatus / useTeslaEnergyLiveStatusHistory /
refreshTeslaEnergyLiveStatus → the /tesla/energy-sites/{siteId}/live-status[/history|/refresh]
endpoints). The page reproduces the web chrome (title + subtitle + refresh-from-Tesla button), the
status badges (grid / storm / backup / last-update) with a >2-minute staleness chip (ADR-013), the
four live-power StatCards (Solar / Battery / Home / Grid with Charging/Discharging/Importing/Exporting
units), the Battery-State panel (SoC value + gradient bar + energy-remaining + total-capacity) and the
Power-Flow-Diagram panel (directional flow arrows incl. the conditional grid-services arrow) — each
with its own honest empty state — and the two history charts (Power-Over-Time TSAreaChart +
Battery-SoC TSLineChart) framed by TSChartContainer and the history RangePicker, polled in real time
via a lifecycle .task loop. All from the P2 design tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled
glass, no direct Charts/recharts, no WKWebView). Every data source implements loading/empty/error/
success; all 33 visible strings resolve from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (zero
hardcoded copy). SI watts/watt-hours format at the render boundary (the endpoint serves SI; nothing
stored or computed non-SI). Adaptive across macOS (regular) and iPhone (compact) via ViewThatFits +
horizontalSizeClass.

Verified GREEN: placeholder gate (0), swiftlint --strict (0 in 8 files), and — with the pre-existing
out-of-scope module poison temporarily neutralized — the macOS app-target whole-module compile with
ZERO diagnostics in every PowerFlowDashboard file and in the two navigation-registration edits. The
ONLY thing standing between this and a green `xcodebuild build`/`test` is pre-existing, out-of-scope
repository breakage (duplicate symbols/filenames in StatusApiDocsPage / ScheduledExportsPanel /
TirePressureUnit / HeroStatus) plus a beta macOS 26.5 SDK that crashes on the repo's DEBUG #Preview
code — none of it caused by, coupled to, or within the allowed scope of this parity unit. Per the
honesty covenant the full build/test gate is therefore reported BLOCKED rather than claimed green.

